{"title":"What I’ve been reading","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/914102264/0/marginalrevolution~What-Ive-been-reading.html","date":1740982054000,"content":"<p>1. Eric Topol, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Super-Agers-Evidence-Based-Approach-Longevity/dp/1668067668/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1ERIOO1IIAKMO&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.AiqOJDnBbHRdlMrW1BfZuw.__NxlMc45lopOFkvtZExLReUsE2rKUGVvgoteDMjrMI&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Super+Agers%3A+An+Evidence-Based+Approach+to+Longevity&amp;qid=1740931052&amp;sprefix=super+agers+an+evidence-based+approach+to+longevity%2Caps%2C74&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Super Agers: An Evidence-Based Approach to Longevity</a>.  Longevity research goes mainstream!  Very clearly written, well argued, and focused on the science.  I cannot pretend to evaluate the details of the material, but this seems a step ahead of the other, typically less serious books on the same topic.</p>\r\n<p>2. Daniel Dain, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/History-Boston-Daniel-Dain/dp/1942155611/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2E4DFKHRV81MG&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.OLyPZTNLxb8NmNuKMn93qEZqy7rT1YpJMpCWvojFA_Aw0IwbKYNtPwTyNiEQ6TOWtdgcolIMCNHVkN_jDVh4sZX8Xde6I1_hc4pFmGpO4ef0trlHISvWTN8hzFPk566AUsgRz0l4e5FK9XN1qDS6ztfY4sr7dnEiSsSdyxKVxEcB70OlCVt4rRFvZwDy44a2MfCm-EuIUswjcB97UOCOq-IW-fr3kOfuu93PD8NMNjw.xvxq2Oyrj3fjoM1DpIcNyfT7AoVliL9fE-s0ya9cCwM&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=A+History+of+Boston&amp;qid=1740931093&amp;sprefix=a+history+of+boston%2Caps%2C66&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">A History of Boston</a>, 772 pp., clearly written and consistently interesting.  Most of all one receives the sense of Boston as a place with a long history of radical ideas.  Has it moved away from that tradition or cemented it in?  I find that more and more of America has little acquaintance with New England and its history, and this book is one good way to remedy that.  Remember Rt.128?  Paul Revere?</p>\r\n<p>3. Stephen Macedo and Frances Lee, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Covids-Wake-How-Politics-Failed/dp/0691267138/ref=sr_1_1?crid=OXJEKAM0FR6N&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.GNq_FWMF4fs_QhSRvM5mIQ.sghpdqGwBqe4vyWC21nn9jXhQ4X5el1YQIisNdlG29I&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=In+Covid%27s+Wake%3A+How+Our+Politics+Failed+Us&amp;qid=1740931133&amp;sprefix=in+covid%27s+wake+how+our+politics+failed+us%2Caps%2C120&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">In Covid’s Wake: How Our Politics Failed Us</a>.  A reasonable, evidence-based, non-crazy account of governance failures and excesses during the Covid crisis.  For me there was not so much new here, but I am glad to see saner voices moving into the discourse.</p>\r\n<p>4. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Wilton-Diptych-Making-Meaning/dp/1857090365/ref=sr_1_1?crid=5N6817VA24L1&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.3uBJv9YChaOI5H_QCj3y6DZcfQqQ6Eih1NY2u4b7BvU.9qyQdlNps9kFziHWv4Ynnht5Zt-ccVQQJ5rsIR8vJDQ&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Making+and+Meaning%3A+The+Wilton+Diptych&amp;qid=1740931176&amp;sprefix=making+and+meaning+the+wilton+diptych%2Caps%2C60&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Making and Meaning: The Wilton Diptych</a>, National Gallery of London.  If you want to learn about a historical figure (in this case Richard II), read a book about an art work associated with them.</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Wilton.jpeg\" width=\"254\" height=\"198\" /></p>\r\n<p>5. Zaha Hadid, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Hadid-Complete-1979-Today-English-French/dp/3836572435/ref=sr_1_1?crid=8IWG80XD89YZ&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.1EP2lRMr4jxg-Jvk_SAUoHxKSm8O-R2wSRDyNenaE3ve9qY5F3KGrJN7C_0uOIfp93T4sTTz34wwJeFFljpXuQEgIx-vkzVp8e-L_e2z5Ax_FTiy011BHyUgsnfrrE_MP42tWLFqltben-6L34vjuitjH1U6HOcm3j6N4ISrxHRrwFRkLovTuRNvEbtT2A__1YnL1vEyaCYeeR2YherVxZtFwZ32ZoFV5dMcgf0sZts.W5me69A_90ChYm56MWJuClPs4_i7bHtZ1kXs-SCurQ0&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=zaha+hadid+Complete+Works+1979-Today&amp;qid=1740931228&amp;sprefix=zaha+hadid+complete+works+1979-today%2Caps%2C85&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Works 1979-Today</a>.  Architecture, plus excellent preliminary sketches of the works.  <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.google.com/search?q=zaha+hadid+weil+am+rhein&amp;sca_esv=a8822ba01c419370&amp;source=hp&amp;ei=yYDEZ8vGOoKw5NoP-ICJwQw&amp;iflsig=ACkRmUkAAAAAZ8SO2lTzrT8-zeBXd5P7qlomcqsDQOfe&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiLz6ax4uuLAxUCGFkFHXhAIsgQ4dUDCBo&amp;uact=5&amp;oq=zaha+hadid+weil+am+rhein&amp;gs_lp=Egdnd3Mtd2l6Ihh6YWhhIGhhZGlkIHdlaWwgYW0gcmhlaW4yBRAAGIAEMgYQABgWGB4yBhAAGBYYHjIGEAAYFhgeMgYQABgWGB4yBhAAGBYYHjIGEAAYFhgeMgYQABgWGB4yCBAAGIAEGKIEMggQABiABBiiBEj_H1AAWM4acAB4AJABAJgBdaABtAyqAQQyMy4xuAEDyAEA-&amp;sclient=gws-wiz\" target=\"_blank\">The Weil am Rhein works</a> are my favorite of what I have seen by her.  Exactly the kind of picture book that will become more valuable in an age of strong AI.  Here are <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.architecturaldigest.com/gallery/zaha-hadid-greatest-works-slideshow\" target=\"_blank\">seventeen buildings by her</a>.</p>\r\n<p>John McWhorter, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Pronoun-Trouble-Story-Seven-Little/dp/0593713281/ref=sr_1_1?crid=9T4ZX3MPKTA0&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.PUIyS-fTf64kMsj1oXLB5A.eFPBhsQU4d6UBEdQeD-wkCxebd9ANEVQfeVzS2pgAD0&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Pronoun+Trouble%3A+The+Story+of+Us+in+Seven+Little+Words&amp;qid=1740931334&amp;sprefix=pronoun+trouble+the+story+of+us+in+seven+little+words%2Caps%2C106&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Pronoun Trouble: The Story of Us in Seven Little Words</a>.  Mostly about actual pronouns, not the PC debates.</p>\r\n<p>There is Paul Bluestein, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/King-Dollar-Future-Dominant-Currency/dp/0300270968/ref=sr_1_1?crid=PRA0ROSARVCL&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.KvC-zM_Gsu2eF8XVXDkotQ.NAbbuK9rQy2v_ucVenpqZgOuu1ZFCRxa1kQiS-BePyU&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=King+Dollar%3A+The+Past+and+Future+of+the+World%27s+Dominant+Currency&amp;qid=1740931382&amp;sprefix=king+dollar+the+past+and+future+of+the+world%27s+dominant+currency%2Caps%2C67&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">King Dollar: The Past and Future of the World’s Dominant Currency</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/what-ive-been-reading-267.html\">What I’ve been reading</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/914102264/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/914102264/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/914102264/marginalrevolution,https%3a%2f%2fmarginalrevolution.com%2fwp-content%2fuploads%2f2025%2f03%2fWilton.jpeg\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/914102264/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/914102264/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/914102264/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/what-ive-been-reading-267.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marg